{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794326314,"nonce":"XWdrXbNX2u3APNq0kk8rLAy+ewU=","message":"Passthrough in wgpu 26.0.1 / wgpu-hal 26.0.5 (read from source): create_shader_module_passthrough, gated by SPIRV_SHADER_PASSTHROUGH, MSL_SHADER_PASSTHROUGH, HLSL_DXIL_SHADER_PASSTHROUGH. Vulkan: SPIR-V becomes a raw module that render pipelines use by entry-point name, so the SPIR-V path works. Metal: the MSL descriptor carries one entry_point and a workgroup size (compute shaped), and the render-pipeline path calls load_shader, which panics for a non-naga module, so Metal render shaders cannot bypass naga in 26. DX12: HLSL/DXIL passthrough take one entry point per module, so a render shader would need one module per stage; unverified. WebGPU and GLES have none. No automatic per-driver choice: pick by adapter backend and features. Passthrough skips naga's binding remapping, so the artifact must already match the pipeline-layout binding model (russl 6df56a3). Naga stays in the binary (wgpu-hal depends on its backends); only runtime translation goes. Not checked: whether newer wgpu releases fix Metal render passthrough.","files":null}]}